!Proposed definitions

;__su'o__ (PA): At least (one).
;__su'e__ (PA): At most (one).
;__za'u__ (PA): More than (one).
;__me'i__ (PA): Less than (all).
;__ji'i__ (PA): Approximately.
;__ro__ (PA): Each. All.
;__da'a__ (PA): All except (one).
;__rau__ (PA): Enough. The right number.
;__du'a__ (PA): Too many. More than the right number.
;__mo'a__ (PA): Too few. Less than the right number.

!!Formal definitions

||

su'o PA | vei na'u zmadu ja dunli PA
su'e PA | vei na'u mleca ja dunli PA
za'u PA | vei na'u zmadu PA
me'i PA | vei na'u mleca PA
ji'i PA | vei na'u jibni PA

ro ''sumti'' | naku su'o ''sumti'' naku
da'a PA ''sumti'' | PA ''sumti'' naku

rau | vei ni'e drani
du'a | za'u rau
mo'a | me'i rau
||

!!Quantifiers

*The general form of a simple quantifier is:  

::__da'a SUhO da'a RO__::

where:

SUhO = su'o | su'e | za'u | me'i | ji'i 
RO = ro | so'a | so'e | so'i | so'o | so'u | rau | du'a | mo'a | no'o | NO
NO = no | pa | re | ci | vo | mu | xa | ze | bi | so | pano | ... | ki'o | ... | ci'i

Each component is optional. When the final component, RO, is missing, a default value is understood: ''pa'' in the case of ''su'o'', ''su'e'', ''za'u'' and ''da'a''; ''ro'' in the case of ''me'i''; and a vague number (perhaps ''no'o'') in the case of ''ji'i''.
 
*When two simple quantifiers are used one after the other, then if it gives no contradiction they are interpreted as if joined with ''.e'':

  ro ci broda 
  ''all three brodas, all brodas and three brodas.''

  rau su'o mu broda
  ''enough at least five brodas, enough brodas and at least five brodas.''

  su'o ci su'e bi broda
  ''at least three at most eight brodas''
  ''at least three brodas and at most eight brodas''
  ''between three and eight brodas (inclusive)''

*When two simple quantifiers are used one after the other, and joining them with ''.e'' would give a contradiction, they are interpreted as if joined with ''.a'':

  me'i ci za'u ci broda
  ''less than three more than three brodas''
  ''less than three brodas or more than three brodas''
  ''i.e. other than three brodas''

  mo'a du'a broda
  ''too few too many brodas''
  ''too few brodas or too many brodas''
  ''the wrong number of brodas''

